course: dictionary
lesson: 8572
title: Scent: a smell, a trail, and a verb
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A scent is a smell. It can be a pleasant smell, like a flower, or a smell that an animal or person leaves behind. Context tells you which one. «Police forces use dogs to track people, because these breeds are good at following a scent.» A dog cannot follow a pleasant flower smell across a field, so here scent must mean the trail a person leaves behind.
explain: «A snake smells with its forked tongue, touching scent to a special organ in the roof of its mouth.» Swap your meaning into the sentence: "touching smell to a special organ" still makes sense, so scent here means the tiny smell particles the tongue picks up. The swap check works well with scent.
explain: Scent can also be a verb, a doing word. «The dog scented a rabbit» means the dog smelled or noticed a rabbit. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try "smelled" in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: A scent is a smell, especially one that is left behind or easy to follow.
fact: «Scent» can also mean perfume, a liquid that makes you smell nice.
fact: Dogs can follow a scent, so a trail of scent can help them find people or hidden things.
fact: «Scent glands» are special places on an animal's body that leave scent behind.
fact: As a verb, «scent» means to smell or notice something, as in «The dog scented a rabbit».
exercise: «Police dogs can follow a scent to track people.» What is a scent here? | A bright coloured flower | * A smell left behind that a dog can follow | A kind of pet food | A sharp, cold wind
exercise: «The dog scented a rabbit in the long grass.» What does scented mean? | Chased away | * Smelled or noticed by its nose | Bit | Heard a loud noise
exercise: Kofi says scent only means a nice smell, like roses. Is he right? | Yes, scent always means a pleasant smell | No, scent means a loud sound | Yes, scent is only ever a verb | * No, scent can also mean a smell an animal leaves behind, which dogs can follow
test: In the phrase «pick up the scent», what might a hunting dog do? | * Follow a smell trail | Bark at the moon | Sleep under a table | Pick up a stick to play
test: Which sentence uses scent as a verb? | The scent of roses filled the room | A scent gland is found on the paw | * The dog scented the rabbit in the grass | Perfume is sold in small glass bottles
exam: What does a snake do with scent, according to «A snake smells with its forked tongue»? | Keep its skin dry | * Touch scent to a special organ in the roof of its mouth | Chase and catch flies | Sing to attract a mate
